<http://data.silknow.org/object/176df054-06ff-3332-a025-582ed676c6fc>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Embroidered Coffer or Box\nSpanish; late seventeenth century\nEmbroidered in silks\nGiven by Señor Piaño [sic]\n1007-1873\n\nA professionally embroidered chest made as a presentation piece. Although intended to be shown, it would have contained valuables of all kinds including documents. [circa 1998]"@en , "Wooden coffer covered with canvas, embroidered with flowers in coloured silks and metal thread. The lid is arched; the sides are studded with brass nails, and it has brass handles."@en , "embroidered, late 17th century, Spain"@en ;
